<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 9 August, from 48 BCE to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pompey" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pompey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/48">48 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,978 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Caesar defeats Pompey at Pharsalus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s veterans routed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>'s larger army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a>. Pompey fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, where he was murdered, and Caesar became master of the Roman world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/378">378 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,648 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Goths destroy a Roman army and kill Emperor Valens at Adrianople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gothic cavalry and infantry overwhelmed the Eastern Roman army near Adrianople in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, killing Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a> and much of his force. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> was never again able to expel the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> from its territory.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1173">1173 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">853 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Construction begins on the bell tower of Pisa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Work started on the campanile of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> Cathedral. Soft ground made it lean by the time the third storey was built, and it became famous as the Leaning Tower of Pisa.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US bomber drops an atomic bomb on Nagasaki</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The plutonium bomb Fat Man exploded over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a>, killing some 40,000 people at once and many more later. Six days later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> announced its surrender.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1969">1969 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Manson Family members murder Sharon Tate and four others</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Followers of Charles Manson killed actress Sharon Tate, who was heavily pregnant, and four others at her <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/los-angeles">Los Angeles</a> home. The murders horrified America and Manson became a byword for evil.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1974">1974 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gerald Ford becomes president after Nixon resigns</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gerald Ford was sworn in as the 38th president, telling Americans 'our long national nightmare is over'. His pardon of Nixon a month later probably cost him the 1976 election.</p></div></li></ol>
